(412546, 36866, 8522, '<td valign="top">Very nice, but I can''t work out why this is in b&amp;w. I''m sure I would have scored it more highly, as the lack of colour really doesn''t suit this picture. 6</td>', 'Very nice, but I can''t work out why this is in b&w. I''m sure I would have scored it more highly, as the lack of colour really doesn''t suit this picture. 6', '2003-09-08 13:41:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(412548, 36681, 9448, '<td valign="top">Wow there are a lot of butterflies in this challenge.  In terms of the composition of the picture, I think there is probably a bit too much dark negative space and that detracts slightly from the butterfly, especially in the lower right-hand corner of the image.  Depending on what the rest of the image looked like, maybe you could have tried putting the head of the butterfly right in the middle of the image.<br/> <br/>On a more technical note, it looks to me as though the focus is a little bit off.  It seems as though only the lower left part of the butterfly is in focus, and too shallower depth of field seems to take the rest of the butterfly out of focus from there.  Given the very blurry background maybe you could have tried using the unsharp mask at a higher level.</td>', 'Wow there are a lot of butterflies in this challenge.  In terms of the composition of the picture, I think there is probably a bit too much dark negative space and that detracts slightly from the butterfly, especially in the lower right-hand corner of the image.  Depending on what the rest of the image looked like, maybe you could have tried putting the head of the butterfly right in the middle of the image. On a more technical note, it looks to me as though the focus is a little bit off.  It seems as though only the lower left part of the butterfly is in focus, and too shallower depth of field seems to take the rest of the butterfly out of focus from there.  Given the very blurry background maybe you could have tried using the unsharp mask at a higher level.', '2003-09-08 13:43:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(412549, 36340, 8522, '<td valign="top">Do you mean panache? Attention to detail... all parts of the package are important! Shame that there is something in the background a similar colour to your flower which makes the composition less striking. 7</td>', 'Do you mean panache? Attention to detail... all parts of the package are important! Shame that there is something in the background a similar colour to your flower which makes the composition less striking. 7', '2003-09-08 13:44:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(412550, 36726, 6667, '<td valign="top">Ok!  You are the winner!  Nice shot.  Dead or alive?  Legs look a little folded up.  Oh yes. . . trim the nose hairs.</td>', 'Ok!  You are the winner!  Nice shot.  Dead or alive?  Legs look a little folded up.  Oh yes. . . trim the nose hairs.', '2003-09-08 13:44:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(412551, 36681, 6667, '<td valign="top">Needs focus</td>', 'Needs focus', '2003-09-08 13:45:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(412552, 36779, 8522, '<td valign="top">That is just hideous.<br/>Great composition and colour... I''d love to write more but I want that thing off my screen! 7</td>', 'That is just hideous.Great composition and colour... I''d love to write more but I want that thing off my screen! 7', '2003-09-08 13:48:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(412553, 36578, 9448, '<td valign="top">Now that''s a spider macro.<br/> <br/>I''d like to know what your background is (A plate?), as this helps the composition which is great in every way from layout through to the background itself.<br/> <br/>Technically I''d say a tiny bit greater depth of field might have made the hairs on the spider''s legs a little bit clearer.<br/> <br/>Easily the best spider shot I''ve seen yet.</td>', 'Now that''s a spider macro. I''d like to know what your background is (A plate?), as this helps the composition which is great in every way from layout through to the background itself. Technically I''d say a tiny bit greater depth of field might have made the hairs on the spider''s legs a little bit clearer. Easily the best spider shot I''ve seen yet.', '2003-09-08 13:48:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(412555, 36313, 9448, '<td valign="top">Yet another wonderful shot in the challenge, at first I thought I wanted slightly shallower depth of field on the wasp, but then I realised that there was no loss with the greater depth of field that you''ve got.  One thing I would have said, is that wilst the wasp may not have approved a mister would have added to the picture in that the wasp would have looked better with some water droplets on its back.</td>', 'Yet another wonderful shot in the challenge, at first I thought I wanted slightly shallower depth of field on the wasp, but then I realised that there was no loss with the greater depth of field that you''ve got.  One thing I would have said, is that wilst the wasp may not have approved a mister would have added to the picture in that the wasp would have looked better with some water droplets on its back.', '2003-09-08 13:52:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(412558, 36242, 327, '<td valign="top">Amazing to find these shells. They are wonderful and so perfect in their beauty. Too bad we don''t get new skin, I could use it! Nice find.</td>', 'Amazing to find these shells. They are wonderful and so perfect in their beauty. Too bad we don''t get new skin, I could use it! Nice find.', '2003-09-08 13:56:55.000000', NULL, 1),
